        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by holding the highest card among those who did not fold, or by making all others fold.',
          gameplay: '1. After cards are on foreheads, a round of betting occurs (ante, then betting as agreedâ€”limit, pot-limit, or no-limit). 2. Players act in turn: fold, check, call, or raise. 3. Showdown: all remaining players reveal. Highest card wins. Ties split the pot. 4. Optional: play lowest wins, or high-low split.',
          keyRules: [
            "Each player sees all other players' cards but not their own.",
            'Ace is high; no suit order for tie-breakingâ€”tied cards split.',
            'Match-pot variant: players declare stay or drop (simultaneously or in turn); best card of those who stayed wins; others who stayed must match the pot.',
            'With simultaneous declaration, two high-card holders can both drop seeing each other; savvy players may exploit this.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "If everyone folds to you, betâ€”you might have the best hand. If you see several high cards on others' foreheads and they are betting, consider folding.",
          intermediate: "Use opponents' reactions: if someone with a visible King hesitates, they may be worried you have an Ace. Bluff by betting confidently when others show weakness.",
          advanced: 'In match-pot, simultaneous declaration creates a game theory puzzle: two players with high cards may both drop, letting a lower hand win. Predict and exploit.',
          tips: [
            "The 'head dress' effect: your card is visible to everyoneâ€”your only signal is your betting.",
            'In match-pot, staying in is costly if you lose; only stay when you think your card is likely best or everyone else will drop.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
